[[File:M 000.png|thumb|The appearance of all Ancient Eggs' Normal Forms]]
'''Ancient Eggs''' are a class of unit first introduced in [[Version 11.4 Update|Version 11.4]]. There are several common traits across all Ancient Eggs:

*Their Normal Forms all appear as identical eggs covered in soil and vegetation. They all share the same stats and are useless as anything more than inefficient meatshields before hatching.
*Their Evolved Forms don't change in stats, but gain an ability and have the dirt cleaned off to reveal the egg's true coloration, often matching the main trait it targets (e.g., [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Cinnabar Egg: N101]] is [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]).
*Their [[True Form]]s hatch to become proper units with massively improved stats and some new abilities, in addition to what they gained in Evolved Form. They require [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] to evolve.
*The hundreds place digit in each of the Ancient Eggs' "identifier code" corresponds with one of the three ways to obtain one generally:  
**Ancient Eggs with the identifier code of N0XX are directly given as rewards for completing a specific stage, usually Empress' Excavation.
**Ancient Eggs with the identifier code of N1XX are given through Catnip Challenges after completing a certain number of Behemoth Culling stages.
**Ancient Eggs with the identifier code of N2XX are obtained from special event gachas.

